WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.790
1990.

2
00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:06.610
About 72 per cent of the UK's
electricity came from coal.

3
00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:08.710
Nuclear made about 20 per cent.

4
00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.630
Gas, almost none.

5
00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:17.190
In September 2024, the last coal-fired
power station closed: Ratcliffe-on-Soar.

6
00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:20.490
North Sea production peaked in 1999.

7
00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:27.190
In 2025, 43.3 per cent of the
energy used in the UK was imported.

8
00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:30.470
So what replaced coal, and at what cost?

9
00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:31.130
Gas?

10
00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:31.930
Nuclear?

11
00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:33.150
Wind and solar?

12
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.270
Imports?

13
00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:37.790
In this mission, you'll see why
countries try to raise supply,

14
00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:41.450
and track how the UK's
electricity mix changed.

15
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:45.970
Then you'll weigh the costs and benefits
of nuclear power and renewables.

16
00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:48.570
Your mission: find out what replaced coal,

17
00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:51.070
and judge what each choice costs.
